   $q$Which theme do both texts share?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Coaches should always choose one star for every team.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"Running is a more difficult sport than rowing a boat.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"A team succeeds when its members work together closely.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The fastest person on a team should do most of the work.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A team succeeds when its members work together closely.$q$, $q$The coach says "Nobody wins a relay alone," and the poem says the water listens only "when we move as one oar." Sofia's idea of running all four laps herself is proven wrong by the stopwatch.$q$, 'draft', '56bd0145-1b4b-5dbe-936a-5ef7bed48e5b')
