   $q$Amira asks, "Were all these stars here the whole time?" How would the speaker of Text 2 most likely answer, based on the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"No, the stars only come out in the country, which is why I cannot see them here.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Yes, and I can see all of them too, as long as I climb up to my roof at night.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Yes, and my cousin far away can see them, but I am happy with the three I know.","is_correct":true},{"text":"No, my cousin made up the stars, because no sky could ever hold thousands of them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Yes, and my cousin far away can see them, but I am happy with the three I know.$q$, $q$The speaker knows the cousin's sky holds thousands of stars while the speaker sees three through the streetlights, and still keeps those three "like coins." The speaker says "I can find only three" from the roof, so seeing all of them is wrong.$q$, 'draft', 'dbe62968-0873-5568-b7bd-a826d37e3034')
